{
  "about": [
    "The Wiki home's status line on the two clients (criterion 5, mocks 11 ② and 12 ④): the space's entries,",
    "the anchors, and the maintenance run's part in each of its looks (contracts/wiki.contract.json",
    "`maintenance.health`). The web reads this file in `lib/wikiHealth.test.ts` and",
    "`components/WikiMaintenanceStatus.test.tsx`; OrbitKit in `WikiHealthCopyParityTests` (`WikiHealthCopy`,",
    "`WikiHealthLogic`, `WikiHomeContent.statusLine`), so the two ends cannot drift into two sentences.",
    "",
    "Each case is a health read (`GET /api/wiki/spaces/:id/health`) at `now`: `parts` is the maintenance",
    "part as the line draws it — words, tone, mark, link — and `text` the same as one line of text. `line` is",
    "the whole status line on a phone, web and iOS alike (the desktop web adds the review count after the",
    "entries): `entries` of the read, the anchors of `space.rootCommitSha`, then `text`.",
    "",
    "From P9 a case may carry the read's `executor`, `systemModel` and `repo`: while the server executes the account's wiki the line",
    "adds one reason after the look's parts and before its links (contract `maintenance.health.serverReasons`), the first that",
    "holds of: worker not running, unconfigured, key refused, unreachable, then the runner (offline, too old) while maintenance is on",
    "or a repository operation waits. A run the server's job made has no session: its View run opens its row on Activity."
  ],
